meta {
  name: Userinfo
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{auth_url}}/connect/userinfo
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

docs {
  Who the signed-in user is, exactly per the scopes the token was granted: `sub` always, then
  `email`, `name` and `role` as granted. The answer is built from the same destination logic as
  the id token, so the two can never drift — and `perm`/`perm_deny` never appear in either.

  Rides {{access_token}}, which either sign-in request exports. A machine token gets 401
  invalid_token here: there is no user behind it to describe.
}
